WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.800
After long hours at work, even actors need
to blow off steam.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.120
But not even Hollywood's finest are immune
to a good, weird prank — and they can get

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.120
pretty strange.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.249
In honor of April Fool's day, here are some
of the most bizarre on-set pranks.

00:00:14.249 --> 00:00:15.389
Chris Pratt's full Andy

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:20.040
During his time on Parks and Recreation, Chris
Pratt was known to improvise almost constantly.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.300
"I was born at 17 months with a full head
of hair, and a full head of teeth."

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.460
So, during a scene where his character, Andy,
shows up in the buff, Pratt was supposed to

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.510
be wearing flesh-colored undies, which could
be blurred out later.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:40.740
But since It was April Fool's Day, he thought
it would be better just to ditch the undies

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.409
and just go with his birthday suit... without
telling anyone.

00:00:44.409 --> 00:00:45.940
"Baby I'm back!"

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.999
"Thank you so --- oh!"

00:00:48.999 --> 00:00:52.969
In an interview with Graham Norton, Pratt
revealed his motivation for the prank.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:55.770
"To me, it didn't really seem like she was
reacting to seeing my d---.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:58.399
And so I was like, 'I know what I'm gonna
do!'"

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:03.300
Apparently, NBC wasn't thrilled, and he got
a letter from the network reprimanding him

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.300
for his behavior.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.910
He reacted in typical Chris Pratt fashion:
he framed the letter and hung it in his office.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:12.160
J-Law gets bugged to death

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.210
Like most people, Jennifer Lawrence is terrified
of bugs.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.900
Since Hollywood's sweetheart has pretty much
no filter when it comes to sharing things

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.350
about herself, that fact was probably common
knowledge on the set of Hunger Games: Catching

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.350
Fire.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.610
So, of course, her costar Jeffrey Wright thought
it would be funny give Lawrence a blue Tiffany's

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.880
box...with a surprise.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.520
"What was in that?"

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:37.840
"Well, about as many crickets as I could cram
into the box."

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.980
Wright didn't get away without a little bit
of karmic punishment, though.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.490
He went on to say that it was really hard
to stuff a bunch of live crickets in a little

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:49.110
box, so as a result, he ended up with his
very own hotel room plague.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:53.950
Jennifer Lawrence seems to get involved in
more on-set pranks than your average actor.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.790
While shooting American Hustle, Lawrence was
nervous about filming in a graveyard.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:02.050
So her co-stars Christian Bale and Bradley
Cooper had the prop team make a personalized

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:08.000
headstone to sneak into the scene that read:
"Jennifer Lawrence, born August 15, 1890,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.670
died April 1, 1913."

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.330
Lawrence reportedly screamed and said, "That's
MY name!

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.170
Is this just a coincidence, or am I going
to die?"

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:20.100
Her co-stars quickly came clean, and the whole
graveyard scene was cut anyhow.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:24.920
But making someone think about their own fleeting
mortality is always a pretty great joke, right?

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:25.920
Right?

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.620
Fat Damon

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.610
During the filming of The Monuments Men, Matt
Damon was especially serious about slimming

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.640
down for his role.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.420
So, naturally, whenever Damon flew back to
New York during filming breaks, George Clooney

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.790
would take all of Damon's clothes to the wardrobe
department and have them made slightly smaller.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:45.390
Damon couldn't figure out why his clothes
were always too small, causing him hit the

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:46.540
gym even harder.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:51.090
It wasn't until much later that Damon figured
it all out — and only after the psychological

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.650
damage had been done.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.000
"I found that only a few days ago that it
really disturbed you."

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.780
"Yeah, and I didn't, I never said anything
because I thought I was being professional

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.770
and trying to lose weight and it wasn't working."

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:06.460
Even after all of that, Damon says that he
would never try to prank the notorious prankster

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.580
back, saying that he doesn't want to "poke
the bear."

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.870
When you get into a prank war with Clooney,
you might not survive.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.080
Fishing for Leo

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.420
After weeks of playing the victim to Leonardo
DiCaprio's roughhousing on the set of Wolf

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.030
of Wall Street, Jonah Hill felt like he needed
a little retribution.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:26.190
So during the first take of the film's sushi
scene, everything went as planned, and Hill

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.560
ate everything on his plate.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.750
But later, Hill went off script and let DiCaprio
take the last piece.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:34.140
"You gonna eat that last piece of yellowtail,
bud?"

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.140
"It's all, it's all yours."

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.830
Now, imagine doing that 70 times.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:44.540
Hill was familiar with director Martin Scorsese's
penchant for shooting the same scene over

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.540
and over.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.540
And over.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.280
By the end of the night, DiCaprio had eaten
an entire school of yellowtail.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.879
For some, that's a regular night, but for
sushi lightweight DiCaprio, it meant puking

00:03:54.879 --> 00:03:55.940
into a trash can.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:01.180
Of course, after this scene, Hill probably
had more than enough fish for one film.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.560
The Yentl of Doom

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.800
Not even Steven Spielberg is immune to the
lure of on-set pranking.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.720
During a scene in Indiana Jones and the Temple
of Doom, Harrison Ford is tied up and whipped

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.750
by a rather gigantic man.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.379
During one take, rather than employing one
of the bad guys from the film, Spielberg had

00:04:16.379 --> 00:04:20.510
Barbra Streisand show up, fully dressed up
in leather, to do the whipping.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.690
With each lash, Streisand would berate Ford
for his movies

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:32.510
To top things off, Carrie Fisher also shows
up to shield Ford, and give him a kiss.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:33.510
Well played, Spielberg.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.490
Star struck by Viggo

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:40.199
Peter Jackson's sprawling Lord of the Rings
films are beautiful, well-acted, and kinda

00:04:40.199 --> 00:04:41.199
violent.

00:04:41.199 --> 00:04:44.270
That could be why Viggo Mortensen decided
to start a new tradition on set.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:47.650
According to multiple co-stars, Mortensen
head butts people.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:48.650
Hard.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:53.100
It's kind of like his way of saying "hello",
except the phenomenon spread, and caused more

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.480
than a few temporary blackouts on set, like
when Orlando Bloom was clobbered.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.880
"And I'm thinking, 'I might never see again.'"

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:00.880
"Heehee.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:01.990
But I think he enjoyed it."

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:06.490
The tradition followed through all three movies
and the red carpet, and Elijah Wood called

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.930
it "spontaneous, violent love."

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:13.830
When you start calling concussions "love,"
it's time to find new friends.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:14.830
"Ohhh!"

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:15.910
Thanks for watching!

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.490
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.550
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

